{"step_index":929,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-21T19:02:55Z","thinking":"**Investigating Process Completion**\n\nI'm puzzled. It appears Spectra.exe concluded after the navigation finished. I'm digging into `App.xaml.cs` to understand the startup sequence and potential dependencies that might cause this. The goal is to determine the point of execution that causes the program to finish, and why it finished after the navigation was done. I need to trace this control flow.\n\n\n**Analyzing Startup Flow**\n\nI've been analyzing the application's startup process, and it seems WPF generates an `App.Main()` method.  I found that the `Run()` method is called without arguments. I'm focusing on the `OnStartup` override in `App.xaml.cs`. I'm going through the event handlers added and shutdown mode to see how the application exits. Particularly, I'm noting the `Exit` event, where the exit code is written to `spectra.log`.\n\n\n**Uncovering Exit Cause**\n\nI've made a breakthrough. I realized the `MainWindow_Closed` event is crucial. When the main window closes, certain resources are disposed of, like the `_screenShareMonitor`, `_hotkeyManager`, and `_sessionController`. I'm now investigating if `_hotkeyManager.Dispose()` is the root cause. A failing or conflicting hotkey registration could trigger the shutdown. It's likely that a failing `RegisterHotKey` call causes the process to exit immediately.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"\"c:\\\\Users\\\\Arthur Henrique\\\\Documents\\\\GitHub\\\\Spectra\\\\src-csharp\\\\Spectra.csproj\"","toolAction":"\"Viewing Spectra.csproj\"","toolSummary":"\"View Spectra.csproj\""}}]}
